    "en": {
      "name": "Fushimi Inari Taisha",
      "description": "Fushimi Inari-taisha (Japanese: 伏見稲荷大社) is the head shrine of the kami Inari, located in Fushimi-ku, Kyoto, Japan. The shrine sits at the base of a mountain, also named Inari, which is 233 metres (764 ft) above sea level, and includes trails up the mountain to many smaller shrines which span 4 kilometres (2.5 mi) and take approximately 2 hours to walk up. It is unclear whether the mountain's name, Inariyama, or the shrine's name came first.",
      "highlights": ["Culture"]
    },
    "ja": {
      "name": "伏見稲荷大社",
      "description": "伏見稲荷大社（ふしみいなりたいしゃ）は、京都府京都市伏見区深草薮之内町にある神社。式内社（名神大社）、二十二社（上七社）の一社。旧社格は官幣大社で、現在は単立神社となっている。",
      "highlights": ["展望"]
    }
  },
